# User Identity Ports — Architecture Guide

## Core Principle

`idpSub` (JWT `sub` claim) is **auth-internal**. It is decoded in the auth module, translated to `userId`
(app profile UUID) via `IUserLookupPort`, and **never passed raw to any other module**.
All domain modules use `userId` exclusively.

---

## Identity Field Convention

| Field | Type | Where | Who may use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `idpSub` | IdP subject (`JWT.idpSub`) | `AuthUser.idpSub` | auth guards, adapters, token-vault only |
| `userId` | App profile UUID | `AuthUser.userId` | All domain modules — audit fields, access control |
| `userInfo` | `UserInfo` (full profile) | `AuthUser.userInfo` | Any module needing display data from `AuthUser` |

---

## User reads vs writes — who calls what

`IUserLookupPort` is defined in `@nabarun-ngo/nestjs-shared-core` and may be injected **anywhere** — `apps/`, `packages/`, and `shared/integrations/` — for **read-only** user profile lookups. The host registers the adapter in `UserModule`.

`UserFacade` lives in the **host app** (`apps/*/modules/user`). Shared packages **cannot** depend on it — that would invert the dependency graph (package → app).

| Caller location | User profile **reads** | User profile **writes** | Never |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Anywhere** (`apps/`, `packages/`, integrations) | **`IUserLookupPort`** | — | `IUserRepository`, foreign user commands |
| **`apps/`** feature modules & `shared/integrations/` | **`IUserLookupPort`** or **`UserFacade`** query methods | **`UserFacade`** | `IUserRepository`, foreign user commands |
| **`packages/`** (`nestjs-shared-*`) | **`IUserLookupPort`** (host registers adapter) | Not supported — fire domain event or require host orchestration | `UserFacade`, `IUserRepository`, foreign user commands |
| **`UserModule`** (provider) | Implements **`IUserLookupPort`** via adapter; exposes **`UserFacade`** | Handlers use `IUserRepository` internally | Export `IUserRepository` to other app modules |

**Prefer `IUserLookupPort` for simple reads** (`findById`, `findByIds`, `findByIdPSubs`). Use **`UserFacade`** when you need orchestrated user operations (list with filters, create, update, delete) or when handler invariants must run via the bus.

**Specialized user read ports** (e.g. `IUserDonationScheduleReadPort`): provider-owned read-only ports for domain-specific data not on `IUserLookupPort` / `UserFacade`.

---

## Three-Port Decision Guide

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| Look up user(s) by app UUID | **`IUserLookupPort.findById` / `findByIds`** — anywhere |
| Find user by IdP subject | **`IUserLookupPort.findByIdPSub`** — or **`GetMyProfileQuery`** with `{ userId?, idpSub? }` in user module |
| All members of a role | **`IUserRolePort.findIdPSubsByRole`** → **`IUserLookupPort.findByIdPSubs`** (or **`AuthFacade.getUsersByRole`**) |
| Grant/revoke/list roles programmatically | **`AuthFacade`** — never CommandBus directly |
| Create/update/delete user profile (`apps/` only) | **`UserFacade`** — never `IUserRepository` or foreign user commands |
| Create/update/delete from a **package** | Not supported — host event or app handler via **`UserFacade`** |

**Cross-module rule:** `IUserLookupPort` is **read-only** and may be used **anywhere**. Mutations in the app go through **`UserFacade`** → bus → handler. See `module-facade-boundary.mdc`.

---

## Port Locations

```
src/core/domain/ports/user-lookup.port.ts      ← IUserLookupPort + UserInfo (host app implements)
packages/nestjs-shared-auth/src/domain/ports/user-role.port.ts       ← IUserRolePort (AuthModule provides, do NOT implement in host)
packages/nestjs-shared-auth/src/application/services/auth.facade.ts  ← AuthFacade (AuthModule provides)
```

---

## What NOT to Do

```ts
// ❌ NEVER read user.idpSub outside auth
const userId = user.idpSub;   // wrong — sub is gone, use user.userId

// ❌ NEVER use idpSub in audit fields outside auth
createdBy: user.idpSub     // wrong — use user.userId ?? user.idpSub

// ❌ NEVER implement IUserRolePort in the host app
// IUserRolePort is provided by AuthModule — it queries authUserRole/authUserRoleGroup tables

// ❌ NEVER import Prisma types into IUserLookupPort
// The port returns UserInfo — a pure TypeScript interface with no Prisma dependency

// ❌ NEVER pass idpSub to correspondence or any other non-auth module
// All cross-module user references MUST use userId (app profile UUID)

// ✅ IUserLookupPort — read-only, inject anywhere (apps, packages, integrations)
@Inject(IUserLookupPort) private readonly userLookup: IUserLookupPort

// ❌ Package — inject UserFacade (app-bound, creates package → app dependency)
constructor(private readonly userFacade: UserFacade) {}  // wrong in packages/

// ❌ Cross-module — inject IUserRepository or dispatch foreign user commands
@Inject(IUserRepository) private readonly userRepo: IUserRepository  // wrong outside UserModule
```

---

## Correct Audit Field Pattern

```ts
// In controllers and command handlers:
const auditId = caller.userId ?? caller.idpSub;

// In auth controllers, use the private helper:
private auditId(caller: AuthUser): string {
  return caller.userId ?? caller.idpSub;
}
```

---

## Consuming App — Registration Template

```ts
// UserModule (host app):
@Module({
  providers: [
    UserFacade,
    { provide: IUserLookupPort, useClass: UserLookupAdapter }, // for packages + auth
  ],
  exports: [UserFacade, IUserLookupPort], // IUserLookupPort for any consumer; UserFacade for app writes
})
export class UserModule {}

// UserAdapter implements IUserLookupPort:
@Injectable()
export class UserAdapter implements IUserLookupPort {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<UserInfo | null> { ... }
  async findByIds(ids: string[]): Promise<UserInfo[]> { ... }
  async findByIdPSub(idpSub: string): Promise<UserInfo | null> { ... }
  async findByIdPSubs(idpSubs: string[]): Promise<UserInfo[]> { ... }
}

// AppModule — wire everything:
AuthModule.forRoot({ ... }), // registers IUserRolePort + AuthFacade automatically
UserModule,                   // registers IUserLookupPort
CorrespondenceModule.forRoot({ ..., imports: [AuthModule, UserModule] }),
```

---

## Caching Reference

| Call site | Cached? | Where |
|---|---|---|
| `UserAccessAdapter.resolve(idpSub)` → `IUserLookupPort.findByIdPSub` | Yes — TTL from `userAccessTtlMs` (default 30 min) | `CacheService` inside `UserAccessAdapter` |
| `ApiKeyVerifierAdapter.validate` | Yes — TTL from `apiKeyTtlMs` (default 30 min) | `CacheService` inside `ApiKeyVerifierAdapter` — `IUserLookupPort` not called |
| `SubscriptionResolutionService` dispatch path | No — hits port fresh per dispatch | Consuming app's `UserAdapter` may add own cache |
| `AuthFacade.getUsersByRole` | No | Consuming app's `UserAdapter` may add own cache |

---

## Breaking Changes (from old `sub`/`userSub` approach)

- `AuthUser.idpSub` → `AuthUser.idpSub` — update all `user.idpSub` reads
- `AuthUser.claims` → `AuthUser.idpClaims` — update all `user.claims` reads
- REST URL `auth/rbac/users/:sub` → `auth/rbac/users/:idpSub` — clients must update
- `UserRoleResponseDto.userSub` → `idpSub` — Swagger schema changed
- DB columns: `auth_user_role.userSub` → `idpSub`, `auth_user_role_group.userSub` → `idpSub` (migration required)
- `IUserQueryPort` and `USER_QUERY_PORT` are **removed** — replace with `IUserLookupPort` + `IUserRolePort`

---

## Justified Exceptions

- `token-vault` uses `ownerSub` — IdP-bound by design, accepted exception
- Within `auth` guards and adapters, `idpSub` is the local identifier — that is intentional
- **User aggregate stores `idpSub`** — persisted on `user_profile`, exposed in `UserResponseDto`; required for IdP linking and admin views
- **`GetMyProfileQuery`** — accepts `{ userId?, idpSub? }`; prefers `findById(userId)`, falls back to `findByIdPSub(idpSub)` when profile UUID is not yet on `AuthUser`
- **`AuthFacade.getUserRoles(idpSub)`** — auth RBAC tables are keyed by IdP subject; pass `user.idpSub` (or `UserInfo.idpSub` from lookup) when calling auth from other modules
- **`IUserRolePort` → `IUserLookupPort` role expansion** — `IUserRolePort.findIdPSubsByRole()` returns `idpSub[]`; comparing or resolving via `idpSub` in integration adapters is correct
- **`workflow-user-resolution.adapter`** — `canUserActOnTask` compares `user.idpSub` against role members — required by auth port API
- **DMS `storageOwnerId`** — app profile UUID (`userId`) for per-user storage providers; shared-bucket providers ignore it
